[statement]
Placing a package reaches a package of the set whose condition names it;
where the walk has not reached that package, a name it provides leads to
a package of the set answering the name that its condition does not name:
placing `uis` reaches `uiso` (`i:openrc uis`), which provides `dev`, and
`bmo`, which provides `dev` too, is walked next, though the repository
lists `uiso` first: its dependency `openrc` is placed, which completes
`uiso`'s condition, so `uiso` goes before `bmo`, all before `eudev`.
The shape of postmarketOS's devices, whose `postmarketos-base` pulls in
`udev-init-scripts` and, through `postmarketos-base-openrc`,
`busybox-mdev-openrc`.

[repository]
P:pb
V:1
D:ramdisk init

P:initramfs
V:1
p:ramdisk=1
D:udev

P:pbo
V:1
p:init=1
D:bmo uiso

[repository]
P:uiso
V:1
p:dev
i:openrc uis

P:bmo
V:1
p:dev
D:openrc

P:eudev
V:1
p:udev=1
D:uis

P:openrc
V:1

P:uis
V:1

[request]
pb

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
install uis 1
install openrc 1
install uiso 1
install bmo 1
install eudev 1
install initramfs 1
install pbo 1
install pb 1
